QmClient
--------

QmClient is graphic tool to browse the configuration of Pirelli/ADB Routers.
QmClient is written with the Qt 6 framework to be
platform independent, both Linux and Windows are supported (OS X coming soon).

QmClient connects to the CPE cm daemon with a tunneled SSH connection,
there is no need to recompile cm or do manual relaying from cm.

Prerequisites to build QmClient are CMake, Qt 6 and libssh2
("cmake qt6-base-dev libssh2-1-dev" on Debian/Ubuntu,
"cmake qt6-qtbase-devel libssh2-devel" on Fedora).
Compilation is straightforward as "cmake -B build ; cmake --build build"

If you're running Qt on Unbuntu with Gnome3 or KDE, perhaps you won't see
Menu Bar. If this is the case, it's a bug in appmenu-qt5, try this workaround
"export QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=".
(https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/appmenu-qt5/+bug/1307619)
